# Axb Optimus

> An Optimus-class humanoid built around predictive echo: predict, act, hear, correct. No full world map.

## Purpose
Explain the robot as a loop that moves on a guessed bounce, then fixes the guess. Source: fitzyracing1/axb-optimus.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Predict the echo.
2. Act on that guess.
3. Restart a virtual sound card on every echo.
4. Hear the real return and correct.
5. Keep mission, telemetry, and an internet proof next to the loop.

## Key ideas
- Predictive echo (guess the bounce first)
- No world map (the robot does not carry a full model of the world)
- Virtual sound card restart (each echo starts hearing clean)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/axb-optimus
predict_echo()
act()
restart_sound_card()
hear(); correct()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. predict_echo() → “guess the bounce”
2. act() → “move on the guess”
3. restart_sound_card() → “clear hearing for the next echo”
4. hear(); correct() → “listen and fix the guess”

## Decisions the program makes
- If the real echo mismatches → correct the hypothesis
- If a map is requested → refuse; the loop does not keep one

## What a person would notice
A robot that lives in a short hear-and-fix cycle.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/axb-optimus and run one cycle.
